WEBVTT

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:07.020
I made contact with him last night, but he ran away.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.820
Don't underestimate Bagbear.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.450
He's as good of a fighter as me, if not better.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.820
Even unawakened, he could be trouble if we aren't careful.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:21.040
And we still don't know what type of singularity he has.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:25.500
Then jumping into that ring was a mistake.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.590
It seemed like so much fun, I couldn't help myself.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.590
Well, we went through all the trouble of bringing the Bakuretsujuu here.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.680
We should finish this today.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.100
We just have to lure him out.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.890
The <i>Magus</i> incident...

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:43.430
Was it a year ago?

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.360
What have you been looking at?

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.230
I was just thinking that it never hit the news.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.410
Didn't I kill a guy with my singularity last night?

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:06.120
Are you really okay, Mr. Haruhiko?

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:23.730
All the laughter, all the tears—everything happened just to meet you

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.430
Always go

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.850
On my own

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.070
Always go

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:42.700
The wind blows my overflowing tears away (the wind blows them away)

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:50.080
I try to reach out my hand time after time toward what's to come

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:56.170
I've been hurt before by careless words

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:05.100
It's time I move forward with that unchangeable past

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.640
All the laughter, all the tears—

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:18.240
everything that has happened brought me to you

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:24.330
All we have left is the future

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:30.710
Please become our reason to continue living

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:37.470
And then the sun will once again shine on us

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.140
Hey, Vice Commander...

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.310
Was there an earthquake late last night?

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.430
I haven't received any reports about one.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.690
A strange tremor shook the arena last night,

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.520
just as the lights went out.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:59.070
Could it have been the Designer's Child's singularity?

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.660
According to our investigation,

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:05.950
that arena uses a collection of illegally captured boys.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:11.870
How powerful is a Planetary Gear's singularity?

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.000
You know, you have a singularity too.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.670
Before your first launch,

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:22.180
weren't you able to sense how terrifying the Kill-T-Gang are?

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.680
I think that's a type of singularity.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.180
That's the Livlaster's power.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:32.400
Why do you call your Livlaster "DC," Teppei?

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.070
It's not short for Designer's Child, right?

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.190
"DC" stands for "Dream Catcher."

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.320
"Dream Catcher"?

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.030
Like those talismans that keep nightmares away?

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.500
It's caused my bad dreams to stop.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:58.130
Are you still having bad dreams?

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:02.590
Yes, every night...

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:06.680
But I have nightmares when I'm awake, as well.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:11.020
Haruhiko being my fiancé is one of them.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.400
It was your father's decision.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:20.070
My father only sees people as tools.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:23.860
My biggest nightmare of all is the fact

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.660
that my father is buying and selling children!

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:30.080
I'm sorry.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:33.160
I don't have any right to say that, do I?

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.420
After all, I...

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.210
was the one who bought you.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.420
I did just what my father does.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:50.060
I'm grateful to you, Miss.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.400
You gave me a place to belong.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.110
Baku...

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.240
This city is where you belong.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.630
Baku, please.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.260
Will you show me that trick again?

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:37.440
This was my only picture of my mother...

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:41.900
My father found it, and tore it up.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.370
Baku?

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:03.960
Here.

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:11.510
What did you do?

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:13.890
A magic trick.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.150
Please... You can do it, right?

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:39.710
Hey, would you be able to use that trick

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:44.170
to restore the ace of hearts alone?

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:50.760
Unfortunately, I don't have that level of control.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:58.140
Hey, that isn't really a magic trick at all, is it?

00:06:56.390 --> 00:07:01.400
My Town

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.070
Well done, Teppei!

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:17.040
Hitting a stationary target is nothing to brag about.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.080
Well...

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:22.580
It seems even that's a bit much for the captain.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.540
Sorry.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.090
I've never practiced shooting.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:30.840
Then you're doing better than expected in real fights.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.220
Hey, Captain...

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.680
Why don't you try it with your Livlaster next?

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.360
No matter how many times I see that, it's still strange.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:55.870
The Science Chief says that you aren't firing the Livlaster,

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:59.410
but rather it's firing itself, through you.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.290
How does shooting with it feel?

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:07.170
It doesn't feel like the Livlaster's controlling me or anything.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.300
Right?

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.300
Yeah.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.630
It feels more...

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.010
Natural, I guess.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.100
Natural?

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:22.230
Well, you don't look at your right hand and think, "This is my right hand," do you?

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.900
Your right hand's just a part of you, so it's only natural for it to be there.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.150
There's no distinction between me and the Livlaster.

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.030
The two of us are both "me."

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:32.900
When I fire the Livlaster,

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:37.870
it feels more like throwing a boomerang

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.540
than shooting a handgun.

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:42.960
That certainly is a singularity.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:46.540
Yes, this is Rita.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.590
Yes. Yes...

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.340
Got it.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:54.010
That was Akari.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:55.760
Hana had another premonition.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.300
Tonight, a Machine Goodfellow will activate.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.640
That arena seems like the best place to look.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:02.270
Yeah.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:06.350
Isn't the Nebula Engine at Haneda, aboard the Regenbogen?

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:12.360
For strategic reasons, we're making preparations to send it here.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.150
But for now, we'll have to rely on the captain.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.450
Roger.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.950
C'mon, let's go one-on-one again...

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:24.370
Hey, that's against the rules!

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:27.710
Oh... H-Hello, Mr. Kariya!

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.670
Business seems to be booming.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:33.170
Yes, thanks to Baku.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:36.010
He's our cash cow.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.180
I see.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.180
Tonight, milk him for everything he's worth.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:40.760
Huh?

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:44.930
This will be the last time we see him in the ring.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.020
Then starting tomorrow, have someone replace him.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:52.360
Does... that mean...

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:54.820
Roger!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.070
Of course! I'll do as you say!

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.790
Hey, Teppei...

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:06.460
What? What's wrong?

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.750
I'm going to run to the bathroom.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.710
Are you okay, Captain?

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.800
Bathroom, bathroom...

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:31.900
Hey.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.450
This corridor is off-limits to unauthorized persons.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.120
Sorry, I was looking for the bathroom...

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.080
You're the champion, right?

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.920
You're strong...

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:56.420
But aren't you afraid of fights without rules?

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.130
I'm not afraid of fighting.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:06.220
I'm afraid of being unable to
protect what's precious to me.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:18.240
And there's the gong!

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:25.200
Our undefeated emperor, Baku, faces off against the Great Ramdes!

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:27.580
A fierce battle has begun!

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:27.580
Amarok and Moco aren't here...

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:29.080
Maybe we were wrong?

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:32.670
Whoa!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.340
The Great Ramdes begins by pulling out wooden swords!

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.340
But melee weapons aren't against the rules!

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:47.810
He stops the swords mid-swing, with his bare hands!

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.320
His strength is amazing.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.610
Maybe it really is him.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.870
He seems different, somehow.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:15.000
The strength to want to protect something, huh?

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:28.350
Anything you want to say, Baku?

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:31.930
I have one thing to say to you.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:35.560
This is my town!

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:42.400
That was Miss Kumiko's voice...

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:43.530
You bastard—

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:53.160
Baku!

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:58.930
Eyecatch

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:09.050
Baku!

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.270
Thanks for coming.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:14.230
Let her go.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:16.190
Slow down there.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:20.690
Agree to our terms, and we'll release her here.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.360
I promise.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.190
What are you after?

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:25.950
Who are you people?

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.280
It'll all be clear soon.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:29.620
Baku...

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:34.710
All right.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:39.960
Don't move, Bagbear.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.590
It'll be over soon.

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:45.300
Now, let's continue what we started last night.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.060
You're free to go, Miss.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.870
So that's what you've been up to.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:31.050
Miss!

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:34.640
Miss!

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:35.270
Sir!

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.390
Hey, why is he alive?

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:45.940
I was shot... but I'm still alive...

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.820
My wounds are nearly gone.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.200
I see...

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.040
So I was right.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:07.510
I always wondered about that
strange magic trick of yours.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.590
This is weird.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.180
What do you mean?

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.930
Do you remember the <i>Magus</i> incident?

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.680
When a ship was blown up in Yokohama, right?

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.270
Yup.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:22.810
An Asanoda ship was blown up.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:25.270
What's strange?

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:30.610
Most of the Asanoda were aboard the ship when it exploded,

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.660
and yet none died.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.120
Is that possible?

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.660
Someone's feelings activated a singularity.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.130
Someone's singularity.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:51.930
I was in the depths of despair from the world that surrounded me.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:01.980
At least go out and say hello, Kumiko.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:06.690
Miss, that's not a bomb, is it?

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:07.610
It is.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.070
It was in our basement.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.070
Don't do anything stupid.

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:14.030
Everyone's aboard the ship tonight.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:19.370
I can put an end to your child trafficking right here.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:20.700
Stop it!

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:44.560
The dream I have every night is reality, after all.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:49.190
You're the reason I'm alive, aren't you?

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:55.070
But it's okay now, Baku.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:17:00.330
I just wanted to protect you.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:02.870
Please, Baku...

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:07.040
Release me from this nightmare...

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.170
What is this?

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:17.180
What kind of trick was that?

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:19.550
When the <i>Magus</i> exploded,

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:23.270
everyone in the Asanoda Yakuza died.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:29.560
In order to revive her, Baku also had to bring back everyone else who died.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.530
I know you are a special person.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:39.070
Live in a way that lets you see the true light...

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:50.750
They're like an illusion Bagbear created.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:56.760
You can't bring back the dead with a singularity.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:59.340
They die because they aren't complete humans.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:01.970
You remember now... Right, Bagbear?

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:03.470
Let's do this!

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.940
Yeah, I understand!

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.020
Fine...

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:11.060
This planet is a nightmare.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:14.570
I'll devour it all!

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:19.530
Machine Goodfellow Bakuretsujuu, activation.

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.740
Abreaction!

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.580
MM bus signal detected.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.880
Identifying epicenter.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.840
Initiating launch sequence.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:13.590
Captain, ready?

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:14.670
Go ahead.

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:18.340
Earth Engine Ordinary, launch!

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:38.280
It's time for the face-off between the Bakuretsujuu and the Earth Engine.

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:42.610
Looks like the Earth Engine's starting off with a deadly weapon.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:45.200
But ranged weapons are against the rules.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:01.090
That's our Bagbear.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:03.590
He's overwhelming the Earth Engine.

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:13.980
The way he's fighting...

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:17.860
It's the champion!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:23.490
He's strong...

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:39.960
If you keep running, you'll run
out of time, Manatsu Daichi.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:49.890
I've got nothing left.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.320
He's very fierce, but...

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:06.450
Why?

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:07.950
I don't feel any strength...

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:13.460
I have nothing left to protect!

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:44.570
Good work, Captain.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:48.700
Sorry, I broke it again.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.490
I'm just glad you're safe, Captain.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:54.750
Do you know who the Designer's Child on board was?

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.120
I think it was him.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:59.040
Him?

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:02.050
The champion.

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:03.260
That strong person?

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:06.800
He was tough, but...

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:08.260
I don't know...

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:11.510
It almost felt like he wanted to die.

00:22:15.140 --> 00:22:17.940
Was it Bagbear?

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:25.400
What's this? It's cute.

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:26.530
Don't touch it!

00:22:28.570 --> 00:22:30.780
What's with the attitude?

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:33.200
What are you looking at?

00:22:33.910 --> 00:22:35.370
My town.

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:36.160
Huh?

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:41.460
My town, huh?

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:55.020
The gentle breeze sweeps away even tears

00:22:55.020 --> 00:23:00.440
Even the recollections of the way of the stars

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:05.320
aren't always good things

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:12.950
I met you again on that faraway day

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:22.420
Even though we're as close as we are, this distant day is beginning

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:30.720
You can hear my voice calling out when I'm all alone

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:36.640
More than just love, it's hard to put into words

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:42.480
I'm searching for what to say while I walk beside you

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:45.610
Instead of saying goodbye,

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:53.740
I'll just put these love spun tears in my right pocket again tomorrow

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:57.160
Love is spreading across the world

00:23:57.160 --> 00:24:03.290
And I finally found it, by your side

00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:18.220
A premonition reveals that there won't be any Machine Goodfellows for a while,

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:20.600
so following Akari's suggestion, we take a vacation.

00:24:21.520 --> 00:24:27.400
But the Planetary Gears still attack Tanegashima, in a way none of us expected.

00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:31.070
Next time, on episode 14 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:31.070 --> 00:24:33.700
A Maiden's Tear That Sparkled Through the Night.

00:24:31.070 --> 00:24:33.700
A Maiden's Tear That Sparkled Through the Night

00:24:34.240 --> 00:24:36.570
Earth Engine, scramble!
